          "item": {
            "@type": "NewsArticle",
            "headline": "Cloudflare cuts 1,100 jobs citing AI efficiency gains even as revenue hits record high",
            "articleSection": "Job Evolution",
            "abstract": "Cloudflare announced its first large-scale layoff, eliminating approximately 1,100 positions predominantly in support roles, with CEO Matthew Prince attributing the cuts directly to AI-driven efficiency improvements. The company simultaneously reported record-high revenue, making it one of the clearest corporate admissions yet that AI is displacing workers even in financially healthy firms. The announcement underscores a growing pattern where AI productivity gains decouple job retention from business growth.",
            "url": "https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/08/cloudflare-says-ai-made-1100-jobs-obsolete-even-as-revenue-hit-a-record-high/",
            "publisher": {
